# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course workspace provisioning: files that must never reach a repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The scripts themselves contain no secrets. Every GUID in them is a published
# Microsoft first-party application id, and there is no client secret, password,
# or key anywhere in the source. What is dangerous is what the scripts write
# beside themselves at runtime.

# The cached sign-in. This holds a refresh token, which is a bearer credential.
# It is DPAPI-encrypted and therefore useless on another machine, but it is still
# a credential and has no business in version control.
.tokencache.xml
*.tokencache.xml

# The run log. With RedactEmailsInLogs set to $false, this contains student email
# addresses in cleartext. A class roster is an education record under FERPA, so
# this must not be committed, published, or shared.
logs/
*.log

# Modules staged by Save-Module. Large, machine-specific, and reconstructible on
# demand, so there is nothing to gain by committing them.
modules/

# Local configuration overrides, which are where a real tenant id or a private
# app registration's client id would end up. Neither is strictly a secret, but
# both are identifying, and the point of an override file is that it stays local.
config.json
config.local.json
*.local.json

# Python variant, if it is kept alongside
.venv/
__pycache__/
token_cache.bin

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
